       iibbvv__rreerreegg__mmrr(())  Modifies  the  attributes  of an existing memory region
       (MR) _m_r.  Conceptually, this call  performs  the  functions  deregister
       memory  region followed by register memory region.  Where possible, re‐
       sources are reused instead of deallocated and reallocated.

       _f_l_a_g_s is a bit-mask used to indicate which of the following  properties
       of  the memory region are being modified. Flags should be a combination
       (bit field) of:

